you for the opportunity to share my experience as this has been a long journey my intention of pursuing this matter the past five years has never been with will ill with the city so rather with an open heart planning attempt to create a win-win situation for all as no good has ever come from the harm of another as a former teacher I learned the most effective way to solve problems is to be aware of potential problems and create a solution before they manifest it was with this attitude that I constantly was on the phone or talking in person with former mayor Kayson simons construction company the many people who were overlooking the project as they continually switched often and

others were sent to communicate with me when I approached mayor Kayson for the first time I had some questions about what was going to happen I'm going to kind of break this down into three parts the before said tutoring and the after of construction and my main concern was losing my front parking and when I had asked the mayor Kayson he said that I would still have my front parking because again I'm looking on going house this whole thing look so right after that about two weeks later he called me back and said you're gonna lose your front parking immediately at that point I became very proactive because I knew that that was going to create issues I parked in front of my house probably 99% of the time in the 14 years I lived there prior to the roundabout the side parking very seldom did I ever parked there and

when I did park there you still had time to get in and get out because you had the stoplights but I knew safety was going to become a concern not just for me but for my family for my clients who would come to my tent to my house to my friends anyone that was going to come and have a connection with me I knew they were going to be jeopardized as far as parking because it's very dangerous I also had conversation with the gentleman that was in charge of Simon construction at the time who was no longer there his name was John we even went to lunch and we finally met with the mayor with Kevin Mayer excuse me Jason with John from Simon's construction with the city engineer who's no longer the city engineer now and

