thus you're in those shoes you really don't understand what that entails I would leave my house or I would come back and I look outside and every time I would go out there I said why am I the only one walking around without a construction hat on when everybody else there has a construction hat there were drenches in my front yard four or five feet deep there was equipment left out the majority of the time I was on the phone with the mayor well where am I going to park there was no designated parking and then I there were times they made a space just south to park I had to park across the street but even getting in and

out of my house and I have a roommate that lives in the basement the access to get into our house there was construction work left everywhere there were a time I came home and they were actually using my water they had their hose hooked up to my house and I simply asked you know what is the deal there they're not paying my bill but yet they're still using that the other things that became a factor as I was talking to the Sanitation Department constantly we should be best friends for as many times as we've communicated and it's still an issue where are we going to put the trash where are we going to pick it up it's not safe for me it's not safer for the city workers the winters are harsh getting in and

out of there but during construction I had to move in and out constantly and I'd have to wait because they always had construction or something one of their trucks or something another was constantly going on to leave and I remember this so clearly I still get a little choked up but I remember one time attempting to back out and I had to wait about ten minutes before they moved everything and I was on my way to my mom's funeral and so this was during a time that I was going back and forth from my house from my mom's house from taking care of her and I just wanted to go home and get a good night's rest I couldn't even do that it was on Sundays that construction started at 6:00 and

I would be talking to former americaís Singh and he said no there's a time wreck they shouldn't be starting till feet and these are just a lot of the little things that had happened you know along the way well after construction anyone who's been in that vicinity it sometimes takes me or five six minutes to get out of my house and I there I have to plan my schedule at times around the time when traffic isn't as aggressive like around five o'clock when it's always where's cars coming and going there's one thing that you never ever get used to and I'm still not used to him yesterday is a prime example it's hearing those cars crash has been constant they may have said that in the beginning there were a few no it's still constant and

this is four years later than 1/2 years later yesterday I was in the living room and I heard it wasn't as loud and I was a bit confused when I walked outside cars were stopped and there was a gentleman sitting out on the side by the curb with the backpack and I'm thinking was this a pedestrian they got hit but then he had a helmet there was a utility car in front a navy blue one and as I walked forward I realized that his motorcycle was completely underneath the car and it reminded me of when I was actually breaking my yard on the corner underneath my tree I had my back because that's how most people rake to the roundabout and

I hear a huge crash and I turn and see a motorcycle going underneath and I thought to myself I am not even safe doing my yard work but to see that yesterday and I made sure he was okay my driveway again was blocked because the cop cars were there they pulled the other car up there so if I had to go anywhere I'd have to wait until they were completely finished with that I made sure he was okay which we've done several times if you look outside my front kitchen window you can see the roundabout it's that close and I want you to think about this there's a roundabout north of town there's a roundabout south of town there are no houses near those roundabouts and

those are single lane roundabouts it just didn't make sense to me why my house being in the vicinity that it has been is that close to the roundabout my great-niece was looking out the kitchen she moved in with me my mom was was taking care of her before she passed and she moved in with me the first night she was there she's in the kitchen looking out the window it's about ten thirty quarter to 11:00 at night and I hear oh my god oh my gosh and I run in the kitchen I'm like what was the next thing you go you look out the window and there was a truck that went was heading east on Pershing that didn't even yield and

